  "id": "caudal",
  "term": "caudal",
  "definition": "Caudal means toward the back or posterior end of a brain structure along its front-to-back axis. In the hippocampus, the caudal portion refers to the posterior part, which earlier studies have linked mainly with spatial memory and navigation.",
